WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:05.860
Hey, this is Presh Talwalkar, and you're watching Mind Your Decisions.

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:09.860
Consider a rectangular array of circles.

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:14.969
We'll fill in some of these circles to make a mathematical expression.

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:28.600
It currently reads (10 + 11)(10 - 11) = 100 + 1!.

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:32.620
But this is not currently a valid equation.

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:36.960
The challenge is to color four blue dots,

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:41.480
or erase four blue dots to make a valid equation.

00:00:42.489 --> 00:00:48.569
I thank Professor Peer Johannsen at Pforzheim University for creating this puzzle

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:51.400
Can YOU figure it out?

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:58.240
Give this problem a try and when you are ready keep watching the video for a solution.

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:14.860
So, how can we make this into a valid equation?

00:01:16.299 --> 00:01:22.559
The amazing answer is that we're going to make each eleven into a 1 times i.

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:26.670
We need to erase a total of 4 dots.

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:30.150
In each of the 11s, we're going to erase 2 dots.

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:38.490
For example, in the first 11 we erase this dot and then this dot and in the second 11, we do the same thing

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:50.720
So now the left-hand side becomes (10 + 1i)(10 - 1i).

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:58.760
When we expand this out, we get 100 + 10i - 10i - i².

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:06.540
This simplifies to be 100 - i², which is equal to 100 - (-1),

00:02:07.509 --> 00:02:14.600
which then becomes 101,
which is exactly equal to 100 + 1!.

00:02:17.140 --> 00:02:21.600
The solution is complex, but the answer is quite real.

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:24.120
Did you figure it out?

